## Why Teams Use Collaborative Workflows

In professional software development and game design, version control is more than an individual backup system—it is a collaborative framework. Without a deliberate, shared workflow structure, teams run into persistent development bottlenecks:

*   **Unresolved Merge Conflicts:** When multiple programmers modify the same core codebase or binary assets simultaneously, Git cannot automatically combine the changes.
*   **Corrupted Production Builds:** Committing untested or partial code directly to the primary codebase can introduce breaking bugs, stopping work for the entire studio.
*   **Untraceable Development Histories:** Chaotic commit patterns make it nearly impossible to determine *why* a mechanic was added or to isolate and revert a game-breaking bug.

Implementing a standardized Git workflow protects the project's health by ensuring that all code is isolated during development, systematically reviewed, and thoroughly vetted before deployment.

